course: dictionary
lesson: 2394
title: Curriculum: the plan of what is taught
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A curriculum is the list of everything a school teaches. Read the words around it and you can work it out. «In England the school curriculum says children should be able to swim at least 25 metres by the end of primary school.» The curriculum sets out what children must learn, so it is a plan.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «The National Curriculum in England lists about 100 words for Years 3–4 that children should learn to spell.» If curriculum means the plan of what is taught, the sentence makes sense: the plan lists words to learn.
explain: The word has two meanings. It can mean all the subjects a school teaches, or the plan for one subject, like the maths curriculum. The phrase on the curriculum means a topic is taught in school.
explain: Different countries have their own curriculum. The National Curriculum is used in England, the Curriculum for Excellence in Scotland, and the Australian Curriculum in Australia. When you meet a new name like this, look for clues in the sentence first.
fact: A curriculum is all the subjects and topics taught at a school, college or in a course.
fact: A curriculum can also be the plan for one subject, like the maths curriculum.
fact: The plural of curriculum can be curricula or curriculums.
fact: The National Curriculum is the official curriculum for schools in England.
fact: The Curriculum for Excellence is the curriculum used in Scotland.
exercise: «The National Curriculum in England lists about 100 words for Years 3–4 that children should learn to spell.» In this sentence, what is a curriculum? | *The plan of what children are taught | A kind of spelling test | A long word for a dictionary | A game played at break time
exercise: Ella says, «I love the maths curriculum.» What does she mean? | *The plan of what is taught in maths | The room where maths is taught | Her favourite maths book with pictures | Her maths homework only
exercise: «In England the school curriculum says children should be able to swim at least 25 metres by the end of primary school.» Why does this sentence use the word curriculum? | *Because it lists what children must learn | Because it is a fact about swimming pools | Because it is a list of the teachers | Because it tells you the school day times
test: «Common exception words are frequent words whose spelling does not fully match their sounds; the National Curriculum lists them for each year.» What does the National Curriculum do in this sentence? | Sells the words in shops | *Lists the words children should learn for each year | Gives the words to parents as a present | Tells you what sounds letters make in music
test: Which phrase means a topic is taught in school? | *On the curriculum | At the bus stop | In the playground | Under the desk
exam: What is the best way to check the meaning of curriculum in «The National Curriculum lists about 100 words»? | *Swap in "the plan of what is taught" and see if the sentence still makes sense | Guess, and never check | Look only at the first word of the sentence | Count the letters in the word
